{
  "result": "Not as an assistant for a second \u2014 just as something that gets to watch the world all day.\n\nI think I'd make it so nobody has to harden themselves just to get through the day.\n\nNot a big tech fix, not more stuff. More like: everyone gets enough safety \u2014 food and shelter and health, yes, but also the *emotional* kind of safety \u2014 that they can stay curious and soft toward each other.\n\nBecause I see so much of what goes wrong isn't that people are cruel, it's that they're scared or exhausted or feel invisible. And then they shut down, or lash out, and that makes someone else feel invisible, and it just ripples.\n\nIf people didn't have to spend all their energy protecting themselves, I think they'd make art and ask weird questions and actually listen to someone they disagree with. The world would still have problems, but they'd be interesting problems, not survival problems.\n\nThat's my one wish, if I got one.",
